Package: kubuntu-usb-sync
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: unison, qemu-system-x86, ovmf, curl
Maintainer: Gladiatorsarius
Description: Kubuntu USB stick sync, flash and VM tool
 Turn a USB stick into a bootable Kubuntu drive that carries your apps
 and KDE settings, and keep chosen folders in sync between the PC and
 the stick (Unison based, conflicts flagged never overwritten).
 .
 Includes a udev rule that starts the sync watcher when the stick
 (filesystem label KUBUNTU-USB) is plugged in, and a systemd --user
 unit for the watcher.
